@startuml

title Request-Reply: the reply finds its requester by the inbox the request names

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

participant "requester" as rq
queue "NATS" as bus
participant "replier\n(one of a queue group)" as rp

rq -> rq : create a private inbox
rq -> bus : request on subject S\n(reply-to: inbox; headers: token, correlation id)
bus -> rp : deliver to one member
rp -> rp : verify, check permission, act
alt success
  rp -> bus : reply to inbox (body)
else refused
  rp -> bus : reply to inbox (empty body, X-Error)
end
bus -> rq : the reply
rq -> rq : read X-Error first, then decode the body
note over rq : no reply within the timeout:\nthe request fails; it is never assumed to have done nothing
@enduml
